WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.160 --> 00:00:03.920
We've spent decades treating the human
brain as a biological

2
00:00:03.920 --> 00:00:07.760
computer. And today, we talk about
artificial intelligence as a

3
00:00:07.760 --> 00:00:11.120
digital brain. We use the exact same
words.

4
00:00:11.120 --> 00:00:12.960
We say a machine is learning.

5
00:00:12.960 --> 00:00:14.800
We say it predicts the word.

6
00:00:14.800 --> 00:00:17.120
We say it hallucinates when wrong.

7
00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:20.720
But relying on this interchangeable
vocabulary is a trap.

8
00:00:20.720 --> 00:00:24.960
It's a broken metaphor, actively damaging
clinical psychology and our

9
00:00:24.960 --> 00:00:27.280
ability to assess AI safety.

10
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:31.280
Brains and language models share a
mechanism called predictive coding.

11
00:00:31.280 --> 00:00:34.240
Both guess the world and use error signals
to correct

12
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.920
themselves. But the physical reality is
not identical.

13
00:00:37.920 --> 00:00:41.440
The brain operates bounded by strict
biological limits.

14
00:00:41.440 --> 00:00:45.120
Mathematical logic scales cleanly to
silicon processors.

15
00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:49.040
A biological framework requires a living,
vulnerable body.

16
00:00:49.040 --> 00:00:51.600
The brain does not sit passively in the
dark, waiting

17
00:00:51.600 --> 00:00:54.080
for your eyes and ears to send it
information.

18
00:00:54.080 --> 00:00:57.680
It actively guesses the world into
existence, running ahead of

19
00:00:57.680 --> 00:00:59.920
reality and using sensory data only to
correct.

20
00:01:00.280 --> 00:01:04.920
its mistakes This data visualization shows
that biological cost.

21
00:01:04.920 --> 00:01:08.040
The human brain accounts for just 2% of
total body

22
00:01:08.040 --> 00:01:11.560
weight, yet it burns through 20% of your
daily metabolic

23
00:01:11.560 --> 00:01:15.560
energy. Every single guess is paid for in
glucose.

24
00:01:15.560 --> 00:01:19.400
This process is an organismic prophecy in
an indifferent, dangerous

25
00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:23.080
universe. Constantly projecting what is
about to happen next is

26
00:01:23.080 --> 00:01:27.320
the absolutely cheapest survival strategy
available to any vulnerable living

27
00:01:27.320 --> 00:01:31.960
creature. For humans, prediction is never
a theoretical math exercise.

28
00:01:31.960 --> 00:01:35.160
It is a constant act of survival, funded
entirely by

29
00:01:35.160 --> 00:01:38.680
physical energy. This brings us to
allostasis.

30
00:01:38.680 --> 00:01:42.440
Unlike homeostasis, which reacts to a
physiological problem after it

31
00:01:42.440 --> 00:01:45.960
happens, allostasis is the process of
predicting what the body

32
00:01:45.960 --> 00:01:49.240
is about to need and deploying resources
before the deficit

33
00:01:49.240 --> 00:01:52.440
occurs. Your heart rate climbs a moment
before you stand

34
00:01:52.440 --> 00:01:55.600
up. Your cortisol levels rise just before
your morning alarm

35
00:01:55.600 --> 00:01:58.720
sounds. Your brain acts as an internal
treasurer.

36
00:01:58.720 --> 00:02:03.600
It relentlessly runs a body budget,
auditing your metabolic spend

37
00:02:03.600 --> 00:02:07.600
against the environmental demands it
expects you to face.

38
00:02:07.600 --> 00:02:11.040
When an organism can no longer predict its
own needs

39
00:02:11.040 --> 00:02:13.920
accurately, that budget overruns.

40
00:02:13.920 --> 00:02:17.680
The internal treasurer fails, and the body
pays the debt

41
00:02:17.680 --> 00:02:20.640
through chronic physical wear and tear.

42
00:02:20.640 --> 00:02:25.440
Through this economic lens, psychological
trauma takes on a specific

43
00:02:25.440 --> 00:02:29.200
physical meaning. It is a structural
failure.

44
00:02:29.200 --> 00:02:33.360
The brain's predictive system encounters
an event far too massive

45
00:02:33.360 --> 00:02:36.400
to anticipate, and the system shatters.

46
00:02:36.400 --> 00:02:40.160
The brain learns the world is
unpredictably lethal.

47
00:02:40.160 --> 00:02:44.160
As a result, it begins assigning extreme
threat levels to

48
00:02:44.160 --> 00:02:45.920
minor sensory noise.

49
00:02:45.920 --> 00:02:49.280
A system stuck in this state of
hypervigilance can no

50
00:02:49.280 --> 00:02:54.280
longer afford. to ignore false alarms
Checking every single floorboard

51
00:02:54.280 --> 00:02:58.520
for danger requires a profound, exhausting
amount of energy.

52
00:02:58.520 --> 00:03:01.880
This is a complete and devastating
collapse of a body's

53
00:03:01.880 --> 00:03:07.000
metabolic budget. Large language models
also build highly complex internal

54
00:03:07.000 --> 00:03:11.480
structures to predict the world, but their
underlying physical reality,

55
00:03:11.480 --> 00:03:14.280
their substrate, is entirely different.

56
00:03:14.280 --> 00:03:16.280
This chart shows the difference.

57
00:03:16.280 --> 00:03:20.280
A biological organism pays for errors in
tissue damage, social

58
00:03:20.280 --> 00:03:21.800
rupture, and death.

59
00:03:21.800 --> 00:03:24.760
An AI pays in mathematical loss functions.

60
00:03:24.760 --> 00:03:27.320
The constraints are entirely detached.

61
00:03:27.320 --> 00:03:30.680
The language model operates without
thermodynamic burden.

62
00:03:30.680 --> 00:03:33.560
Its limits are compute power and server
bills.

63
00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:37.000
An artificial network has no continuous
living self.

64
00:03:37.000 --> 00:03:40.280
Because it does not inhabit a physical
body, it completely

65
00:03:40.280 --> 00:03:43.640
lacks the biological imperative to ensure
it survives to see

66
00:03:43.640 --> 00:03:46.960
tomorrow. We can engineer a robot to have
a battery,

67
00:03:46.960 --> 00:03:49.760
but those stakes are externally assigned
by us.

68
00:03:49.760 --> 00:03:54.160
For humans, the stakes are intrinsic,
inescapable, and existential.

69
00:03:54.160 --> 00:03:57.760
A patient told debug a thought is often
left trying

70
00:03:57.760 --> 00:04:00.080
to fix their logic while their body
remains in a

71
00:04:00.080 --> 00:04:02.320
state of high alert exhaustion.

72
00:04:02.320 --> 00:04:06.720
Because the underlying budget crisis
hasn't been addressed, these logic-based

73
00:04:06.720 --> 00:04:09.600
treatments often fail to produce lasting
change.

74
00:04:09.600 --> 00:04:14.000
Real clinical success requires respecting
the body's physical substrate.

75
00:04:14.000 --> 00:04:17.520
It means finding ways to explicitly lower
the metabolic cost

76
00:04:17.520 --> 00:04:19.040
of existing in the world.

77
00:04:19.040 --> 00:04:22.640
Social attachment functions as a
mechanical tool for this purpose.

78
00:04:22.640 --> 00:04:26.160
A safe relationship acts as a buffer that
literally reduces

79
00:04:26.160 --> 00:04:28.560
the brain's anticipated energy spend.

80
00:04:28.560 --> 00:04:32.480
Lasting recovery happens through
physically restoring the body's energy budget

81
00:04:32.480 --> 00:04:33.920
to a state of safety.

82
00:04:33.920 --> 00:04:37.520
The vocabulary we use also distorts our
approach to AI

83
00:04:37.520 --> 00:04:40.600
policy. When we look at a mathematical
misfire in a

84
00:04:40.600 --> 00:04:43.720
language model and call it a
hallucination, we are making

85
00:04:43.720 --> 00:04:45.000
a dangerous choice.

86
00:04:45.000 --> 00:04:49.720
Borrowing words from clinical pathology
accidentally smuggles human vulnerability into

87
00:04:49.720 --> 00:04:53.960
cold statistics. By treating algorithms
like fragile minds, we blind

88
00:04:53.960 --> 00:04:57.400
ourselves to the actual structural risks
these systems pose.

89
00:04:57.400 --> 00:05:00.120
The human brain is a metabolic prophet.

90
00:05:00.120 --> 00:05:04.520
It is tethered to mortality, and its
predictions carry semantic

91
00:05:04.520 --> 00:05:08.200
meaning entirely because of the threat of
death.

92
00:05:08.200 --> 00:05:11.160
The next time someone tells you their
artificial model is

93
00:05:11.160 --> 00:05:15.080
genuinely thinking, ask them what the
machine is physically paying

94
00:05:15.080 --> 00:05:16.600
to have that thought.

